# On-device test settings for `make test-device` / `make test-device-<platform>`.
# Copy this file to tests/devices.env (git-ignored) and fill in the devices you have.
# A platform with an empty host is skipped by `make test-device`.
#
#   <PLATFORM>_HOST      ssh target, e.g. root@brick.local (key-based login: no password prompt)
#   <PLATFORM>_SSH_OPTS  optional extra ssh options, e.g. -p 2222 -i ~/.ssh/trimui
#
# "?=" keeps values given on the command line or in the environment in charge:
#   make test-device-h700 H700_HOST=root@192.168.1.60
#
# The address is never written to the debug bundle.
#
# Optional settings, forwarded to the device when set (environment or command line):
#   SDCARD_PATH          the SD card on the device (default /mnt/SDCARD)
#   TEST_BASE            where the throw-away fixtures go (default $SDCARD_PATH/.core-states-tests)
#   KEEP=1               keep the fixtures (for looking at them afterwards)
#   COLLECT_USER_DATA=1  also copy /States/Cores and /Saves/Cores into the debug bundle (up to
#                        USER_DATA_MAX_KB, default 65536). Off by default: the bundle then has
#                        listings and checksums only. Turn it on when a bug needs the real files.
#   MENU_TESTS=1         also run tests/bats/device-menu.bats (drives the real menu with button presses)
#   PAD_NAME / PAD_DEVICE  the gamepad: the name in /proc/bus/input/devices (default "TRIMUI Player1",
#                        right for tg5040 and tg5050) or a /dev/input/eventN node. Needed for h700 and
#                        my285 when MENU_TESTS=1.
#   PAD_A PAD_B PAD_UP PAD_DOWN  button events as type:code:value (defaults: the TrimUI pad)
#   UI_WAIT (8)  KEY_GAP (0.5)   seconds for the menu to appear, and between button presses
#
# `make test` fails when this file and the platforms in pak.json drift apart: every
# platform there needs both lines below.

TG5040_HOST ?=
TG5040_SSH_OPTS ?=

TG5050_HOST ?=
TG5050_SSH_OPTS ?=

H700_HOST ?=
H700_SSH_OPTS ?=

MY285_HOST ?=
MY285_SSH_OPTS ?=
